# C6: TLS termination for both AgentDash instances (decided 2026-08-16:
# Caddy + mkcert local CA).
#
# HTTPS ports: 3112 → mkboard (:3102), 3113 → uat (:3103). The plain-HTTP
# ports stay bound to keep existing sessions working during the cutover;
# once every client machine trusts the CA and PUBLIC_BASE_URL is flipped,
# the servers should bind 127.0.0.1 so the only LAN-reachable ports are TLS.
#
# Client-machine step (one-time, per person): copy rootCA.pem from
#   /Users/yang/Library/Application Support/mkcert/
# and either run `mkcert -install` with CAROOT pointing at it, or add it to
# the system keychain / cert store manually.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why there are now four site blocks instead of two
#
# `mkmini.local` is mDNS. It resolves on the same physical LAN and NOWHERE
# else -- in particular it does not resolve over Tailscale, because mDNS is
# link-local and the tailnet is a routed overlay. So the original two blocks
# meant HTTPS worked from a desk in the same room and failed from anywhere
# else, while plain HTTP kept working over the tailnet and hid the problem.
#
# Measured before the change: `https://100.64.89.16:3112` and
# `https://yangs-mac-mini.tail112187.ts.net:3112` both returned 000
# (connection refused by Caddy -- no site block matched the SNI, and an IP
# request sends no SNI at all), while `http://100.64.89.16:3102` returned 200.
# Someone connecting over Tailscale would have reached the plaintext port and
# believed that was the intended path.
#
# The certificate was reissued to carry every name this box is legitimately
# reached by. `tailscale cert` would be better -- a real publicly-trusted
# cert for the `.ts.net` name, and nobody would need the mkcert CA at all --
# but provisioning it fails today with an invalid ACME order, which means
# HTTPS is not enabled for this tailnet in the admin console. That is a
# console toggle for the tailnet owner, not something fixable from here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
	auto_https disable_redirects
}

(agentdash_tls) {
	tls /Users/yang/.config/agentdash/tls/mkmini-multi.pem /Users/yang/.config/agentdash/tls/mkmini-multi-key.pem
}

# --- mkboard (:3102) -------------------------------------------------------

https://mkmini.local:3112, https://yangs-mac-mini.tail112187.ts.net:3112 {
	import agentdash_tls
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3102
}

# Reached by IP, which sends no SNI. Caddy needs an explicit block or it
# closes the connection before any certificate is offered.
https://100.64.89.16:3112, https://192.168.86.57:3112 {
	import agentdash_tls
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3102
}

# --- uat (:3103) -----------------------------------------------------------

https://mkmini.local:3113, https://yangs-mac-mini.tail112187.ts.net:3113 {
	import agentdash_tls
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3103
}

https://100.64.89.16:3113, https://192.168.86.57:3113 {
	import agentdash_tls
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3103
}
